\section{LIGO O4 Integration}

LIGO O4 strain data $h(t)$ is encapsulated and injected as:
\begin{equation}
    \Delta \gamma_{ij}(t) = A_{ij} h(t),
\end{equation}
where $A_{ij}$ is a polarization tensor derived from detector geometry.

The strain is decomposed into:
\begin{equation}
    h(t) = h_+(t) e_+ + h_\times(t) e_\times,
\end{equation}
and mapped into the BSSN variables via:
\begin{align}
    \tilde{\gamma}_{ij} &\rightarrow \tilde{\gamma}_{ij} + \Delta \gamma_{ij}, \\
    K &\rightarrow K + \Delta K(h), \\
    \tilde{A}_{ij} &\rightarrow \tilde{A}_{ij} + \Delta \tilde{A}_{ij}(h).
\end{align}

